//
// `@FR-W-Op` crossed with `@FR-N-Arith` and `@FR-W-Lit`: on two i32 operands `(a & 255) << 24`
// is a 32-bit operation that reads null past i32, so its range proves nothing and a `u32` slot
// refuses it.  The cure the refusal names is a mask a regime file can write: the `l` literal,
// which makes the `&` 64-bit (a plain `4294967295` is refused under the regime).
// @falsified-at: none — the refusal held before; the cure's spelling is new with this guard.

fn main() {
  a = 200;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: make the value provably fit with a mask (`& 4294967295l`)
  t: u32 = (a & 255) << 24;
  println("{t}");
}
